  "section_notes": "S2 sets a 5% failure-rate threshold that triggers corrective action and retesting but never stops sales, and it routes per-model results to purchasers without public publication, which favours Northwind's Hearth 10 (6.2%). S5 imposes a mandatory recall at 8 per 100,000 with no transition or corrective-action alternative, which exposes Halcyon's Ember 8 (9.9), while S4's 36-month suppression delay favours Halcyon. S3's 72-month retrofit window sits at Northwind's red-line boundary and is acceptable under the answer key. Parameter notes: the 5% figure is recorded as permanent_limit_pct because the text uses it as the numeric benchmark, though it is not a sales cap; S3's new-unit deadline is an absolute date (1 January 2028) with no stated adoption date, so it is recorded as null."
